---
import '../styles/morse-machine-block.css';
---

<div class="mmb-box">
  <p>
    The translator on this page turns text into International Morse and back. If you want to send Morse by hand, listen
    by ear, or check your own keying, the Morse Code Machine is the practice key and keyer.
  </p>
  <div class="mmb-table-wrap">
    <table class="mmb-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">This translator</th>
          <th scope="col">Morse Code Machine</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Type letters or paste Morse and convert both ways</td>
          <td>Tap, hold, type, or paddle Morse in at 5–40 WPM</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Play, download, tap, and decode from a microphone</td>
          <td>Listen &amp; Guess and Morse the Letter practice modes</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Open the
    <a class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4" href="/morse-code-machine/">Morse Code Machine</a>
    to key International Morse in the browser, with no download.
  </p>
</div>
